Demographic Focus: CKD prevalence is heavily concentrated in the 50–75 age range, suggesting that proactive screening should intensify at age 50.

Screening Protocol: Since a significant portion of positive cases show normal traditional markers, clinics should utilize eGFR and Stage-based analysis for more accurate early detection.

Data Integrity: Addressing the lack of Red Blood Cell (RBC) documentation is vital for a complete clinical picture, as missing data can lead to diagnostic delays.
